@kevin_dorst @ben_golub Uncomputability of the halting problem
Proof: Assume towards contradiction H is algorithm s.t. H(M,x)=1 ⇔ Turing machine M halts on x.

Define D as follows
def D(z):
   while H(z,z):
      pass

D(D) halts  ⇔  H(D,D)≠1 ⇔ D(D) doesn't halt
Hence get contradiction, QED.

